comments.body:
With this setup, analogjs users may cut out `@storybook/builder-webpack5` with their dependency manager of choice themselves - if they want to save some MB of node_modules - as it's automatically installed via https://github.com/storybookjs/storybook/blob/next/code/frameworks/angular/package.json#L62. This could be moved from dependencies to peerDependencies with an added check:

```ts
  if (!resolvePackageDir('@storybook/builder-webpack5')) {
    throw new Error('Peer dependency @storybook/build-webpack5 is missing. Please install');
  }
```

But it felt like it's not my call to make to destroy the "batteries included" nature with a breaking change for the sake of a 3rd party plugin.
